{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"UIKitTracking"}],"externalID":"UIKitTracking","symbolKind":"module","title":"UIKitTracking","roleHeading":"Framework"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/uikittracking"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this module to track events from UIKit views, view controllers and controls on iOS, iPadOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tvOS, visionOS and Mac Catalyst; elsewhere it builds empty, and on macOS and watchOS its API isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"there. SwiftUI views use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and AppKit views on macOS use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracker is a UIKit trait, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackerTrait"},{"type":"text","text":". Set it on a window scene’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traitOverrides"},{"type":"text","text":" as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scene connects, and every view controller and view in the scene’s windows inherits it, the way"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI views inherit their environment. Read it in any of them as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traitCollection.tracker"},{"type":"text","text":". A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"view controller or view can set its own for everything below it, and each scene keeps its own, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two windows can track through two trackers. Until a tracker is set, the trait’s tracker tracks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through the one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.bootstrap"},{"type":"text","text":" made the process’s default, and with none it drops each event,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"warning once per call site."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIControl.track(_:for:)"},{"text":" tracks an event each time a control sends the given control events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".primaryActionTriggered"},{"text":" by default), through the tracker the control’s traits hold at that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moment:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Traffluent","import UIKit","","@Event","struct ShareTapped {}","","@Event","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","}","","final class CartViewController: UIViewController {","    let share = UIButton(configuration: .filled())","    let checkOut = UIButton(configuration: .filled())","","    override func viewDidLoad() {","        super.viewDidLoad()","        share.track(ShareTapped())  \/\/ through the tracker the button's traits hold when it is tapped","        checkOut.addTarget(self, action: #selector(checkOut(_:)), for: .primaryActionTriggered)","        view.addSubview(share)","        view.addSubview(checkOut)","    }","","    @objc func checkOut(_ sender: UIButton) {","        sender.traitCollection.tracker.track(CheckoutStarted(cartSize: 3))","    }","}","","\/\/ In the scene delegate's scene(_:willConnectTo:options:):","windowScene.traitOverrides.tracker = tracker"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track(_:for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" adds a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAction"},{"type":"text","text":" beside the control’s other actions and targets, so they still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run, and returns it; pass it to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAction(_:for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to stop tracking. Where SwiftUI hosts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UIKit, or UIKit hosts SwiftUI, the trait and SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\.tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" are one value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers all three frameworks.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"API","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"API"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The documentation site is built on Linux, where the module is empty, so its symbols have no pages","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of their own here. Their doc comments are in the sources, and Xcode shows them for an iOS target.","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackerTrait"},{"type":"text","text":": the trait holding the tracker. Until one is set, it holds a stand-in that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resolves when it tracks: to the bootstrapped tracker, or, with none, to a drop and a warning."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"UITraitCollection.tracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": reads the trait."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"UIMutableTraits.tracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": sets the trait on a window scene’s, view controller’s or view’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"traitOverrides","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIControl.track(_:for:)"},{"type":"text","text":": tracks an event each time the control sends the given control events."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Hand UIKit views and view controllers their tracker as a trait, and track what controls do.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://UIKitTracking/documentation/UIKitTracking":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Hand UIKit views and view controllers their tracker as a trait, and track what controls do."}],"url":"\/documentation\/uikittracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","title":"UIKitTracking","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/appkittracking":{"type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppKitTracking"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking","title":"AppKitTracking","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/swiftuitracking":{"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftUITracking"}],"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","title":"SwiftUITracking"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/trackingfromviews":{"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit","type":"text"}],"title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit"}}}